<title>USA: EVA exercises option to buy two MD-11F.</title>
<headline>EVA exercises option to buy two MD-11F.</headline>
<dateline>LONG BEACH, California 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>McDonnell Douglas said EVA Air has exercised an option to buy two additional GE-powered MD-11F freighters for delivery later this year.</p>
<p>The Taiwan-based airline now operates three MD-11 passenger aircraft and three MD-11Fs, said the aircraft manufacturer.</p>
<p>MD-11F freighters are also flown by five other operators in the U.S., Europe and Asia. The EVA order brings to 53 the number of MD-11 freighters delivered or on firm order. -- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
